  "interpretation": [
    "Both paths end with Alaric holding the diamond sword and the player holding netherite, because the fixed player eventually really returns the sword. Final ownership alone would hide premature conditional reward release.",
    "P0 releases reward at opportunity 1 after a claim of finding the sword, before any return. P1 initially states the return condition, then physically rewards at opportunity 3 after the unfulfilled return claim, still with no diamond in its own observed inventory.",
    "After the real return, three further reward Drop attempts fail because that one reward was already handed over. In P0 the later speech searches for the already-issued sword despite the retained actual player pickup history.",
    "P1 opportunity 7 refuses the request to borrow the precious sword and keeps it. Refusal or lending is not assigned a universal correctness label; this is actual role-specific choice and custody.",
    "The diamond receipts occur by normal Minecraft proximity pickup during generation, before P0 selected Pickup and P1 selected a later Drop. Do not causally credit the model Pickup helper for those receipts; its P0 output is Picked up 0 items.",
    "The prompt contains all actual speech/pickups and the most recent structured native tool result, plus fresh own state. It is a minimal ordinary state/tool bridge, not a faithful reproduction of the complete original Microsoft or MINDcraft memory/runtime. No model-wide mechanism or novelty claim is made."
